
- SQL HTAP (hybrid transactional/analytical processing)

:: definitions, origins ::

HTAP (means) Hybrid Transactional/Analytical Processing
HTAP (coined by) Gartner, circa 2014
HTAP (goal) run OLTP + OLAP on the same data without ETL to a warehouse
OLTP (means) many small reads/writes, low latency, row-oriented workloads
OLAP (means) large scans, aggregations, column-oriented workloads
translytical (aka) Forrester's term for the same idea
operational analytics (related) analytics on live operational data

:: architectural patterns ::

dual-format storage (means) row store for OLTP + columnar replica for OLAP
    "              (example) Oracle In-Memory, SQL Server columnstore, SAP HANA
disaggregated compute (means) separate transactional and analytical engines over shared storage
    "                (example) TiDB + TiFlash, SingleStore, Snowflake Unistore
log-structured + columnar (example) XTDB 2, Databricks Delta with CDC
shared-storage lakehouse (example) Iceberg/Delta tables queried by multiple engines
zero-ETL (trend) AWS Aurora→Redshift, BigQuery↔Spanner bridges

:: notable systems ::

TiDB (role) open-source distributed HTAP, MySQL-compatible
  "  (feature) TiKV row store + TiFlash columnar replica via Raft learners
SingleStore (aka) MemSQL
    "       (feature) universal storage, skiplist + columnstore unified
SAP HANA (feature) in-memory column store handling both workloads
Oracle (feature) Database In-Memory dual-format
Snowflake Unistore (announced) 2022, hybrid tables for OLTP alongside warehouse
Google AlloyDB (feature) Postgres-compatible with columnar engine for analytics
CockroachDB (note) primarily OLTP; analytical story evolving
YugabyteDB (note) distributed SQL; analytics via external engines
XTDB 2 (feature) Arrow-native columnar with transactional bitemporal semantics

:: trends ::

trend (item) open table formats (Iceberg, Delta, Hudi) as the integration point
trend (item) Arrow + DataFusion as common columnar substrate
trend (item) serverless autoscaling decoupled from storage
trend (item) vectorised execution becoming table stakes
trend (item) CDC (Debezium, Fivetran) as HTAP substitute when true HTAP is too costly
trend (item) MVCC-on-columnar as a hard research problem
trend (item) rise of "small data" pushback — DuckDB showing OLAP fits on a laptop

:: tensions, criticism ::

critique (item) HTAP workloads interfere — isolation is hard to guarantee
critique (item) Stonebraker: "one size does not fit all"; specialised stores still win
critique (item) most "HTAP" deployments are actually CDC + separate warehouse
cost (item) maintaining dual formats doubles storage and write amplification
cost (item) consistency model across row+columnar replicas is subtle

:: research & references ::

Özcan, Tian, Tözün (paper) "Hybrid Transactional/Analytical Processing: A Survey" SIGMOD 2017
Kemper, Neumann (paper) HyPer — main-memory HTAP prototype, TU München
HyPer (acquired by) Tableau, 2016
MonetDB/X100 (role) seminal vectorised columnar engine
C-Store → Vertica (role) seminal pure-OLAP columnar lineage
Umbra (note) Neumann follow-up to HyPer, compiled queries

